<title>FRANCE: ADP export traffic down 1.7 pct in Jan-Sept.</title>
<headline>ADP export traffic down 1.7 pct in Jan-Sept.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>432,504 tonnes of air cargo exports left the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in the first nine months of 1996, down 1.7 percent on the same period last year, airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>North America was the major destination for cargo exports from the Paris airports in the months in question with 118,667 tonnes flown, down 1.2 percent on January-September 1995.</p>
<p>ADP shipments to the Far East/Pacific region, fell by 3.5 percent on 1995 levels to 89,830 tonnes.</p>
<p>ADP January-September 1996 Middle East exports rose by 7.7 percent on the first nine months of last year to 43,219 tonnes.</p>
<p>Global January-September 1996 export traffic in tonnes from the ADP, by region, with percentage change on January-September 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p>    Domestic		  35,316	    down   2.7</p>
<p>    European Union	  50,231	    down   0.5</p>
<p>    Non-EU Europe	    9,389	    down   5.6</p>
<p>    North Africa	     7,905	    down  34.5</p>
<p>    Sub-Saharan Africa    35,211	    up     1.3</p>
<p>    North America	  118,667	    down   1.2</p>
<p>    French territories    19,885	    down   3.6</p>
<p>    Latin America	   22,851	    up     2.0</p>
<p>    Middle East	     43,219	    up     7.7</p>
<p>    Far East		  89,830	    down   3.2</p>
<p>    Total		    432,504	    down   1.7</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
</text>
